DESCRIPTION:🏞️ Lake Summit 10 Mile Trail Race Tuxedo\, North Carolina
  Where mountain views meet lakeside charm Join us for a breathtaking 10-mi
 le run around the sparkling shores of Lake Summit\, nestled in the heart o
 f the Southern Appalachian Mountains\, just south of historic Flat Rock\, 
 NC. This scenic course weaves along packed dirt roads through the quiet co
 mmunity of Tuxedo\, offering runners a peaceful\, nature-filled experience
  you won’t soon forget. 🌄 What to Expect As you circle the lake in a 
 counter-clockwise direction\, you’ll take in stunning views of clear blu
 e waters\, charming lakefront homes\, and the rolling backdrop of the Blue
  Ridge Mountains\, dressed in vibrant fall foliage. With 90% of the course
  on well-maintained gravel roads\, it’s the perfect mix of beauty and ch
 allenge. A single short\n\nMore: https://runsignup.com/Race/NC/Zirconia/La
 keSummit10Mile\n\nSource: RunSignup\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bi
 ke/calendar
LOCATION:1299 Old US 25 Hwy\, Zirconia\, NC
URL:https://runsignup.com/Race/NC/Zirconia/LakeSummit10Mile
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NCCX Pre-Season Skills Clinics 2026
DTSTART:20260913T040000Z
DTEND:20260913T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260817T172753Z
UID:bbf6b38b2e5ea38d@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:clinic
DESCRIPTION:Learn all about cyclocross and the skills needed to compete wi
 th local experts and pro racers\, as well as get warmed up for the upcomin
 g season! Sessions will allow for new and experienced racers alike to prac
 tice and prepare for racing. Women's only clinic is for female athletes an
 d is focused on beginner and new racers. Limited to 25 participants. Coach
 ed by experienced racers\, including U23 elite racer Ada Watson. Clinic ru
 ns 8am-11am. Attendees are invited to bring a bagged lunch and stay for cr
 afts and conversation. Open clinic is open to all levels of experience\, a
 bilities\, and genders. Guest coaching will be lead by retired pro racer a
 nd certified coach Jon Hamblin and other guest coaches. Please be ready to
  ride at 12pm\, clinic will end at 6pm. Bring a snack for a mid-session br
 eak\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/nccx-pre-season-skills-clinic-2026\n\n
 Source: BikeReg\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:35.508641;-82.6130561
LOCATION:125 Idlewood Dr\, Asheville\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/nccx-pre-season-skills-clinic-2026
