BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GTC Upville Mile
DTSTART:20270828T000000
DTEND:20270828T000000
DTSTAMP:20260817T172753Z
UID:e681f27e029816fc@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:Why run down when you can run up ? GTC Upville Mile is a 1-mil
 e\, uphill-only road race in Paris Mountain State Park\, on the steepest p
 art of Paris Mountain State Park Road. The route is one of the toughest\, 
 if not the toughest uphill 1-mile road segments in the Upstate\, including
  nearby Altamont Road\, and the road going up Sassafras Mountain. If you l
 ike a running challenge\, this event may be just the ticket for you. Don't
  be surprised though if you find it necessary to do at least a couple shor
 t walk breaks. It's recommended you practice on this route before you race
  on it. With an average grade of 8.2%\, and elevation gain of 460 feet in 
 just a mile\, it surely will not disappoint. John Hart\, Race Director\n\n
 More: https://runsignup.com/Race/SC/Greenville/GTCUpvilleMile\n\nSource: R
 unSignup\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
LOCATION:2401 State Park Rd\, Greenville\, SC
URL:https://runsignup.com/Race/SC/Greenville/GTCUpvilleMile
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
